item.description:
///mats.rescue.costs&#10;&#10;I am writing as a resident of Shurdington Road to raise concerns about vehicle speeds following the installation of the new roundabout.&#10;&#10;Since its completion, I have observed increased speeding along the straight section towards the next roundabout. The road layout appears to encourage acceleration, raising concerns for pedestrians, cyclists, residents, and animals.&#10;&#10;These concerns are also personal. Our family cat was killed in a hit-and-run shortly after the works, and more recently my partner and I had a near miss while walking our dog when a vehicle overtook at high speed and passed close to us on the pavement nearly colliding with us both.&#10;&#10;Given the residential nature of the area and multiple nearby schools, there is high pedestrian activity, including children walking, cycling, and using scooters on narrow footpaths. This creates a clear safety risk.&#10;&#10;I would be grateful if you could:&#10;&#10;* Investigate whether speeds have increased since the roundabout was installed * Carry out speed monitoring or a traffic survey * Consider measures such as traffic calming, speed signage, vehicle-activated signs, or enforcement&#10;&#10;I believe proactive action is needed to prevent an imminent serious incident with the schools returning soon.
<br>Nearest road to the pin placed on the map (automatically generated by OpenStreetMap): Shurdington Road, Warden Hill, Cheltenham
<br><a href='https://www.fixmystreet.com/report/9916261'>Report on FixMyStreet</a>
